-- title:
--   Principal nilradical and exact vanishing of its powers in a cyclic algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and $A$ a commutative $K$-algebra. Fix $x\in A$ and $z\in K$. Assume every element of $A$ is $q(x)$ for some $q\in K[T]$, and that $q(x)$ is nilpotent if and only if $q(z)=0$.
--
--   Write $t=x-z1_A$ and let $N$ be the nilradical of $A$. Then
--   $$N=(t),\qquad N^k=(t^k)\quad(k\geq0).$$
--   Moreover, $t$ is nilpotent and, writing $\nu=\min\{j\in\mathbb N:t^j=0\}$, one has
--   $$N^k=0\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\nu\leq k.$$
--   The formulas include $k=0$. No finite-dimensionality or characteristic-zero assumption is required.
-- source:
--   Derived supporting algebra for the Senthil Kumar mission. A commutative K-algebra generated by x, in which q(x) is nilpotent exactly when q(z)=0, has nilradical generated by x-z. Its kth power is generated by (x-z)^k and vanishes exactly when k is at least the nilpotency class of x-z. This is inferred supporting algebra. It needs no finite-dimensionality or characteristic-zero hypothesis. Pinned Mathlib revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474: Algebra/Polynomial/Div.lean, dvd_iff_isRoot; RingTheory/Ideal/Operations.lean, Ideal.span_singleton_pow; RingTheory/Ideal/Span.lean, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_bot; RingTheory/Nilpotent/Defs.lean, nilpotencyClass and pow_nilpotencyClass. Primary documentation: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Polynomial/Div.html and https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/Ideal/Operations.html . No new definitions or platform dependencies.

import Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Div
import Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Algebra
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Operations
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Nilpotent.Lemmas

theorem WeierstrassEllipticZeta.polynomial_cyclic_nilradical_powers
    (K A : Type*) [Field K] [CommRing A] [Algebra K A]
    (x : A) (z : K)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (fun q : Polynomial K =>
      q.eval₂ (algebraMap K A) x))
    (hnil : ∀ q : Polynomial K,
      IsNilpotent (q.eval₂ (algebraMap K A) x) ↔ q.eval z = 0) :
    nilradical A = Ideal.span {x - algebraMap K A z} ∧
      ∀ k : ℕ,
        (nilradical A) ^ k = Ideal.span {(x - algebraMap K A z) ^ k} ∧
        ((nilradical A) ^ k = ⊥ ↔ nilpotencyClass (x - algebraMap K A z) ≤ k) := by sorry
